{{also|bohemian}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|Bohemia|ian}}

In sense of [[Romani]] and by association, marginalized artists, from {{etyl|fr}} {{term|bohémien||person from [[Bohemia]], [[Romani]]|lang=fr}}, from {{term|Bohême||[[Bohemia]]|lang=fr}}; compare {{term|gypsy||[[Romani]]}}, from {{term|Egypt}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# {{context|countable}} A native or resident of [[Bohemia]].
# {{context|uncountable}} The [[dialect]] of the [[Czech]] [[language]] spoken in Bohemia.
# {{context|countable|archaic}} A [[Romani]] ([[Gypsy]]).
# {{context|countable|slang}} A marginalized and impoverished young artist, or member of the urban [[literati]].

